ver the radicand is positive." 13194139538751 17592186045443 true] [17592186673264 1080 "y=\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{8}{8 \\cdot C \\cdot e^{4 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right)} + 12 \\cdot \\left(x-3\\right) + 3}}" 13194139538751 17592186045443 true] [17592186673264 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538751 17592186045443 true] [17592186673264 1083 #uuid "b3a8cc80-e0bf-54ce-9bf9-ff81ebc9261f" 13194139538751 17592186045443 true] [17592186673265 1080 "y=\\left(C \\cdot e^{\\frac{3 \\cdot x}{2}} + \\frac{2}{3}\\right)^{2}" 13194139538751 17592186045443 true] [17592186673265 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538751 17592186045443 true] [17592186673265 1083 #uuid "c6af010a-d598-520a-bb6d-0ecb2c8813c1" 13194139538751 17592186045443 true] [17592186673266 1068 #edb/ref 17592186673242 13194139538751 17592186045443 true] [17592186673266 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139538751 17592186045443 true] [17592186673266 1071 "Find the general nonzero real solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}- \\left(x+2\\right)^{2} \\cdot y=- \\frac{3 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{2}}{y^{4}}.\n$$\n\nWork on an interval where $\\left(x+2\\right)>0$. Choose constants and intervals on which the displayed expressions are real and finite.\n\n{{selection}}" 13194139538751 17592186045443 true] [17592186673266 1072 #uuid "c98ebde1-9cae-55b5-a3ae-6eb0a074c80f" 13194139538751 17592186045443 true] [17592186673266 1074 "This is a Bernoulli equation with\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}p(x)&=- \\left(x+2\\right)^{2}\\\\ q(x)&=- 3 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{2}\\\\ n&=-4.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nDivide by $y^{-4}$ and set $z=y^{5}$. The chain rule gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}x}=5 \\cdot y^{4}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}.$$\n\nHence the linear equation in standard form is\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}x}+\\left(- 5 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{2}\\right)z=- 15 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{2}.$$\n\nAn integrating factor is\n\n$$I(x)=e^{\\int - 5 \\cdot \\left(x+2\\right)^{2}\